.TH APPNEST 1 "" "appnest 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appnest \- manage, integrate, and launch AppImages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appnest
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B appnest
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appnest
manages AppImage files: it imports them into a library, creates application
menu entries, desktop shortcuts and icons for them, launches and stops them,
discovers AppImages that are not managed yet, checks for updates published
inside the AppImages, and can calculate their SHA-256 hashes.
.PP
Started without a command, or with file names, AppNest opens its window and
offers to add or run each file. Only one instance runs at a time; files passed
to a second invocation are handled by the running instance.
.SH COMMANDS
All commands work without a display. \fIID\fR is an application identifier as
shown by \fBappnest list\fR.
.TP
.B list
List the applications and whether each one is ready, running, or missing its file.
.TP
.BI "info " ID
Show details of an application: path, size, type, launch method, integration
state, checksum and update information.
.TP
.BI "import " [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
Add AppImages to the library.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-copy
Reference the file where it is instead of copying it into the library.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-menu
Do not create an application menu entry.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shortcut
Do not create a desktop shortcut.
.RE
.TP
.BI "launch " ID " [\fB\-\-\fR \fIARGS\fR...]"
Start an application, passing any arguments after \fB\-\-\fR to it.
.TP
.BI "run " FILE " [\fB\-\-\fR \fIARGS\fR...]"
Run an AppImage once without adding it to the library.
.TP
.BI "remove " [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIID\fR
Remove an application. Asks for confirmation in a terminal.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-delete\-file
Also delete the copied AppImage file.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.RE
.TP
.BI "scan " [\fIDIR\fR...]
List AppImages in the scan folders that are not in the library yet. Without
arguments, the configured scan folders are used.
.TP
.BI "check-update " ID
Check the update information the publisher embedded in the AppImage.
.TP
.BI "update " [\fB\-y\fR] \fIID\fR
Check for an update, then download and install it. Downloads use HTTPS and are
verified against the checksum published in the update information before they
replace the current version.
.TP
.BI "replace " ID " " FILE
Replace the AppImage behind an application with a newer file, keeping its
identity, launch method and integration settings.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version ", " version
Show the version.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for usage errors.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appnest/
Managed AppImages, extracted AppDirs, icons and the application database
(default: \fI~/.local/share/appnest/\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/appnest/config.toml
User settings, including the scan folders (default: \fI~/.config/appnest/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/
Desktop entries generated for integrated AppImages (named appnest-<id>.desktop).
These entries launch through \fBappnest launch\fR so that failure detection and
the runtime fallbacks apply everywhere.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/appnest/launch-<id>.log
Standard error output of the most recent launch of an application.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/appnest/updates/
Temporary location of downloaded updates.
.SH NOTES
Updating downloads the complete new AppImage; the zsync delta-transfer method
is not implemented. Embedded AppImage signatures (.sig_key sections) are not
verified.
